# Art-directed marketing frontend

Use this alternative primary when a marketing/portfolio brief clearly calls for distinctive, experimental or expressive art direction, or explicitly requests this workflow. Ordinary frontend, neutral landing pages and existing-UI redesign/refinement default to `impeccable` under the OpenCode routing policy. Select one design owner, not a stack of competing philosophies; relevant research/motion specialists may assist. User-approved direction and existing brand/stack take precedence over defaults.

## Essential workflow

1. Infer page kind, audience, assets, references, accessibility constraints and preservation mode. State a one-line design read. Investigate discoverable facts first; ask only if a consequential visual choice genuinely diverges.
2. Set design variance, motion and density from the brief; they are contextual, not a universal aesthetic. Read the relevant detailed rules below before applying a technique.
3. Inspect installed dependencies, existing design system and source. Preserve the stack/version and one coherent token/icon system. Never invent an official design-system package or silently install a new framework.
4. Preserve visual assets/content/IA/SEO/analytics in a redesign. Image generation, if available and appropriate to the approved brief, precedes fallback photography; never invent a screenshot or fake production metrics. Disclose missing asset/tool capability.
5. Build semantic responsive source with legible contrast, keyboard/focus states, real interactions, loading/empty/error states, and explicit mobile behavior. Motion must communicate something, respect reduced motion, avoid render-loop state updates, and clean up listeners/GSAP contexts. Keep content visible without a successful animation.
6. Before completion, read and apply the detailed pre-flight matrix to the applicable surface, verify actual build/runtime/browser evidence at appropriate scope, and report unverified limitations. A plausible layout or a checklist alone is not proof.

